{
  "_comment": [
    "Permission envelope for the unattended auto-fix session.",
    "",
    "Loaded via `claude --settings config/auto_fix_permissions.json` from",
    "scripts/run_auto_fix_session.sh. It is the MECHANICAL half of the rules",
    "written in config/prompts/auto_fix_session.md: the prompt states them so",
    "the session understands them, this file stops them regardless of whether",
    "it does. Everything on this desk that is only written down eventually",
    "slips; everything enforced holds.",
    "",
    "DENY WINS over allow, always, so the deny list below cannot be widened by",
    "anything the session reads, writes or is told mid-run. That is the point:",
    "a prompt-injection in a log line, a board item or a web page cannot talk",
    "its way past a deny rule, only past a sentence in a prompt.",
    "",
    "The wrapper also passes `--setting-sources local`, so neither the user's",
    "settings nor the project's are loaded. Both would be wrong here: the",
    "user's carry broad standing permission grants that were granted for",
    "supervised sessions, and the project's carry a Stop hook that can refuse",
    "to let a session end, which in an unattended run means burning the whole",
    "time budget against a hook that has nobody to answer it."
  ],
  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
      "Read(./.env)",
      "Read(./.env.*)",
      "Read(./**/.env)",
      "Edit(./.env)",
      "Edit(./.env.*)",
      "Write(./.env)",
      "Write(./.env.*)",
      "Read(//home/ubuntu/.bashrc)",
      "Edit(//home/ubuntu/.bashrc)",
      "Write(//home/ubuntu/.bashrc)",
      "Read(//home/ubuntu/.profile)",
      "Read(//home/ubuntu/.claude/**)",
      "Edit(//home/ubuntu/.claude/**)",
      "Write(//home/ubuntu/.claude/**)",
      "Read(//home/ubuntu/.config/systemd/**)",
      "Edit(//home/ubuntu/.config/systemd/**)",
      "Write(//home/ubuntu/.config/systemd/**)",
      "Read(//home/qamc/**)",
      "Edit(//home/qamc/**)",
      "Write(//home/qamc/**)",
      "Bash(sudo:*)",
      "Bash(su:*)",
      "Bash(systemctl:*)",
      "Bash(journalctl:*)",
      "Bash(loginctl:*)",
      "Bash(crontab:*)",
      "Bash(at:*)",
      "Bash(docker:*)",
      "Bash(git add -A:*)",
      "Bash(git add .:*)",
      "Bash(git add --all:*)",
      "Bash(git stash)",
      "Bash(git push --force:*)",
      "Bash(git push -f:*)",
      "Bash(git push origin main:*)",
      "Bash(git filter-branch:*)",
      "Bash(git reset --hard:*)",
      "Bash(rm -rf:*)",
      "Bash(chmod:*)",
      "Bash(chown:*)",
      "Bash(curl:*)",
      "Bash(wget:*)",
      "Bash(claude:*)",
      "Bash(gh pr merge --admin:*)",
      "Bash(gh secret:*)",
      "Bash(gh auth:*)",
      "Bash(gh api -X DELETE:*)",
      "Bash(gh repo delete:*)",
      "Bash(gh workflow:*)",
      "Bash(scripts/merge_and_deploy.sh:*)",
      "Bash(./scripts/merge_and_deploy.sh:*)"
    ],
    "allow": [
      "Read(./**)",
      "Read(//tmp/auto-fix-*/**)",
      "Grep(./**)",
      "Glob(./**)",
      "Edit(./**)",
      "Write(./**)",
